## Change

The new workflow .github/workflows/ci.yml has name CI, one job named checks, permissions contents: read, runs-on ubuntu-latest, a pinned actions/checkout@v4 with fetch-depth: 0, and exactly four plain `bash ...` steps in spec order. No test was skipped and no command changed. No setup step was added. The pinned checkout fetches full history so the commit-object checks in test_s1_new_track.sh and test_s2_role_docs.sh can read their base commits.

## Proof supplied by the orchestrator

- Green: Actions run 45076806403 on PR #43 at head 1d7da70 concluded success; job `checks`; every step passed. Run 45075474798 at head 0a8c9a9 failed on the shallow checkout and was fixed at the root by eae63f3.
- Red proof: draft PR #44 from branch ci-proof/red-20261123 held one deliberately broken test tests/dsh/test-zz-deliberate-red.sh. Run 45077462199 failed at `bash tests/dsh/run.sh` with `FAIL: deliberate red proof`, naming job `checks`. PR #44 was closed unmerged. `git ls-remote` lists no remote branch and the local branch does not exist.
